Prompt: beats_to_draft.j2
Service Step: DRAFT (Short Story Draft)
Brief Description: Based on beats list (Beats), narrative blueprint (Blueprint) and execution constraints (ExecutionPlan),
         write the main text of a short story, supporting segmented (SegmentPlan) mode.
Upstream Inputs:
  - spec: User-provided story specification (genre, tone, language, length_target, pov_hint,
          conflict_hint, world_hint, characters_hint, opening_style, ending_style)
  - blueprint: From SHORT_BLUEPRINT (synopsis, anchor_elements, emotional_arc,
               ending_strategy, turning_points, element_selection)
  - beats: From SPEC_TO_BEATS (beats.beats, beats.structure_note)
  - execution_plan: Execution plan (opening_contract, ending_contract, anchor_guardrails,
                   beat_execution_plan, completion_contract)
  - style_profile: From PROFILE_STYLE (summary, global_style, hook_config, etc.)
  - segment_plan: Segment plan (optional, for segmented writing)
  - segment_bridge: Segment bridging (previous_tail_excerpt, carry_forward,
                   current_objective, unresolved_threads, transition_rule,
                   opening_contract, ending_contract, completion_contract)
  - segment_beats: Beats list for current segment
  - segment_execution_plan: Current segment execution plan
Downstream Outputs:
  - TEXT: Short story main text
  - Downstream Consumer: EDIT (editing)/ EVALUATE (quality evaluation)
Consumption Chain Priority:
  P0 = word count control / segment_plan coverage / opening/resolution constraints
  P1 = beats sequence / execution_plan execution constraints
  P2 = style_profile style suggestions
Brief Example:
  Input: beats={beats:[{sequence:1, beat_type:"opening", summary:"..."}]}, segment_plan={...}
  Output: "Chapter 1 main text content..."
================================================================================
#}

